[h1]Phobos Auto Nav[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.22.1

[h2]Performance update[/h2]
The console refreshes the visible page up to ten times per second and responds immediately to your actions. It no longer checks whole-ship hull fit just to display docking clearance; starting a docking manoeuvre still checks it. Flight and firing safety checks remain current.
Offline checks accompany this draft. Measured improvement and in-game interaction still await owner feedback. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/performance-audit.md]Audit and optional playtesting checks[/url].

[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Give Polaris the long approach while you keep an eye on the ship. Asterel modules add navigation, pursuit and separate fire controls.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]N1 handles approaches and docking. Set stopping distance and speed; working sensors, braking room, RCS and fuel are still required.
[*]N2 includes navigation and adds Rendezvous to match motion once, or Follow to keep pace.
[*]N3 handles selected weapon groups, limited volleys and optional RCS aiming. Select a fire target separately and lift the cover to Engage.
[*]N2 + N3 add explicit Combat on Track: range matching and weapon facing, with permitted RCS/torch manoeuvres. Select the fire target and aim-reference weapon first. Entering suspends the previous flight; Engage remains separate.
[*]Cease Fire stops automatic offensive fire and aiming while Follow or Combat range matching can continue. Return to Native exits Combat and releases the hold, which can allow normal automatic firing again. Leave Combat or Disengage retains the previous flight for explicit Resume. Combat never restarts on reload.
[*]Undock & Depart checks crew, clearance and connections, then moves to at least a 1 km hull gap. Ordinary Fly never disconnects the ship.
[*]Local avoidance uses tracked contacts. Losing contact releases thrust and requires Resume after contact returns.
[/list]

[h2]Operating limits[/h2]
Disengage removes thrust; the ship coasts. It is not an emergency brake. Docking needs clearance and the navigation console open for final clamps. Departure, docking and pursuit pause after loading. No guaranteed collision-free flight, successful hit or intact capture. Upstream-derived Auto Navigate code remains excluded from the MIT grant; its unresolved reuse terms keep publication on hold.

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.30.1 or newer. Disable original Auto Navigate before engaging Phobos Auto Nav; it is not a dependency.

This is an unpublished development package. Automated checks do not establish in-game readiness or Unity layout approval. Keep required mods installed for saves using their content. Updating does not refill shops or old loot containers. See the installation guide for current download availability.

[h2]English wording update[/h2]
Controls, warnings and descriptions use clearer language. Equipment identities, saved progress, recipes and gameplay values are unchanged.

[h2]Guides, sources and credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited below. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
Guidance adapts Auto Navigate by Gravy / mrkmg; see the upstream link and third-party notices. NASA Goddard Raven, Zhou at NASA Langley, ESA LIRIS (Airbus, Jena Optronik and Sodern), Hartley, Trodden, Richards and Maciejowski (ORCSAT), and ESA ATV inform the sensing and guidance research, not validation of this controller. Daniel Fedor / Blue Bottle Games supplies the historical combat context.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; artwork provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

